From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: an Escape with no guest manager is not a crash

A plain Escape pressed at a shell with a browser window open took the
whole desktop down, and did it again on the next Escape after the
restart.

A `<webview>`'s page is a guest, so attaching one builds a
`BrowserPluginEmbedder` on the shell's own WebContents --
`BrowserPluginGuest::Init` does it -- and every key the shell's page
leaves unhandled comes back to `WebContentsImpl::HandleKeyboardEvent`,
which offers it to that object first. For a plain Escape, and for no
other key, the object then walks the browser context's
`BrowserPluginGuestManager`. This fork has none: it depends on neither
//extensions nor //components/guest_view, so `ProfileImpl::GetGuestManager`
answers null, and this is the one of the class's four methods that does
not check before dereferencing it. `CancelGuestDialogs` and
`AreAnyGuestsCurrentlyAudible` both do.

`GetFullPageGuest` is the same omission on the same object, reached from
`WebContentsImpl::SaveFrameWithHeaders` rather than from a keystroke, so
it is closed here too rather than left for whoever asks a browser window
to save a page.

NOTHING IS LOST BY RETURNING EARLY. The loop body this skips rejects a
pointer-lock request on each guest, and a guest in this fork cannot hold
one: `WebViewGuest` does not override `RequestPointerLock`, so
WebContentsDelegate's default drops the request and no page behind a
<webview> is ever locked. A guest manager built to satisfy content would
therefore be a manager with nothing to manage.

Upstream's bug rather than the fork's, and written to be filed:
`upstream/browser-plugin-embedder-null-guest-manager.md`. The guard is
`scripts/guard-webview-escape.sh`, which presses the key that crashed.

WRITTEN BY HAND, AGAINST THE SERIES RATHER THAN IN A CHECKOUT, but with
both blobs computed rather than zeroed: no other patch in the series
touches this file, so its pre-image is the pin's and the post-image is
the pin's file with these six lines in it.
---
 content/browser/browser_plugin/browser_plugin_embedder.cc | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/content/browser/browser_plugin/browser_plugin_embedder.cc b/content/browser/browser_plugin/browser_plugin_embedder.cc
index dba1fc61aee1..bb5a5d208d0e 100644
--- a/content/browser/browser_plugin/browser_plugin_embedder.cc
+++ b/content/browser/browser_plugin/browser_plugin_embedder.cc
@@ -50,6 +50,9 @@ bool BrowserPluginEmbedder::HandleKeyboardEvent(
     return false;
   }
 
+  if (!GetBrowserPluginGuestManager())
+    return false;
+
   GetBrowserPluginGuestManager()->ForEachGuest(
       web_contents_, [](WebContents* guest) {
         guest->GotResponseToPointerLockRequest(
@@ -63,6 +66,9 @@ bool BrowserPluginEmbedder::HandleKeyboardEvent(
 }
 
 BrowserPluginGuest* BrowserPluginEmbedder::GetFullPageGuest() {
+  if (!GetBrowserPluginGuestManager())
+    return nullptr;
+
   WebContentsImpl* guest_contents = static_cast<WebContentsImpl*>(
       GetBrowserPluginGuestManager()->GetFullPageGuest(web_contents_));
   if (!guest_contents)
